# LM Salgados → MioDelivery

Authoritative brief for the MioDelivery case study and LM Salgados catalog entries. Do not invent beyond this.

## Core message (visitor-facing)

1. **Partner, not vendor** — first major client (2017→today); immersion in ops before code.
2. **Verbal chaos → shared surface** — shouted “50/100/200” → CorelDRAW production-board sketch (30-min slots, blink/alarm) → live kitchen panel.
3. **Continuous evolution** — basic POS → multi-unit system (**Hi sistemas**, early placeholder name) → pandemic delivery boom (PWA → TV menu → RFID cube + QR) → scale.
4. **Software that grows with the business** — 2 stores + factory → 7 stores / 4 cities (incl. bakery).
5. **Productization** — LM stack → MioDelivery for a **few hand-picked clients** that prioritize quality over quantity; current multi-store UI in the case.
6. **Printing** — early thermal comanda → clearer modern receipt; **print.it** local print server replaces **IdeYouPrint** at LM (fewer limits; used by MioDelivery and other systems).

Do **not** narrate LM logo construction / monogram in the MioDelivery Featured case. Brand identity belongs only on catalog `lmsalgados`.

## Partnership

- LM Salgados was Isaque’s **first major software client** and remains a client **from 2017 to today**.
- Relationship started while Isaque was in college and a frequent customer of the main store next to campus.
- Owners asked for custom management software for **factory + stores** — flexible, multi-unit, matching a very fast food operation.
- Working style: deep business immersion first; follow daily ops; talk to owners and staff; consult on process, not only ship features. Partner, not ticket vendor.

## Operational pain (before)

- Counter orders often meant tens/hundreds of salgados prepared in minutes.
- Kitchen coordination was verbal: staff shouted quantities (“50”, “100”, “200”) to the fry line.
- Needed one integrated multi-store platform with shared real-time information.

## Solutions built over time

- **Multi-unit system** (early brand: **Hi sistemas** — placeholder name thrown up quickly to plant a flag) — orders, clients, products, stores, users; factory + shops on one stack.
- **Kitchen production panel** — first proposed as a **CorelDRAW sketch**: 30-minute squares across store hours; salgado qty on the left, count of orders of that amount due in the slot on the right; scheduled + new POS orders made the square blink and play an alarm. Inspired by McDonald’s / Burger King boards; later matured into today’s filterable kitchen panel.
- Early POS prioritized function over polish; UI matured into a full ERP for LM’s reality.
- **2020 pandemic (delivery boom — stage by stage):**
  - **Isolation** → consumer ordering app + **first production PWA** + **order listing** as the ops surface (heavy filtering by store/category/range, status, pending prints, chat, re-charge, finance footer) — tell it fully here; do not repeat as a later chapter.
  - **IdeYouPrint** (right after) → kitchen had the panel; **delivery riders** needed a **paper sale receipt**. Browsers block silent print; learned **Python**; desktop app beside the printer talks to the **API** and thermal printer so receipts print with **no click**. Origin story lives here.
  - **Distancing / early reopen** → **animated TV menu**.
  - **Return / low contact** → **RFID table cube** (cube logo as brand and hardware) + **QR everywhere**.
- **Current MioDelivery UI** (later chapters): multi-store dashboard; kitchen panel; product catalog + PDF menu; multi-store admin; reports. **Order list**, **TV menu**, **RFID/QR**, and **IdeYouPrint origin** are told under pandemic `steps` — do not repeat those origin stories later.
- **print.it** — final case chapter: local automatic print server UI (Go, built with help from Cursor); at LM replaces IdeYouPrint (origin of IdeYouPrint stays in the pandemic step). No thermal-receipt photo here — UI only.

## Scale

- Start: **2 stores** in one city + factory.
- Today: **7 stores** across **4 cities**; one unit expanded into a large store including a **bakery**.

## Brand (catalog only)

- Heart mark = L + M + heart; marketing site https://lmsalgados.com.br (`lmsalgados`).
- Do not explain the mark in Featured MioDelivery.

